    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554">

                <pb facs="1384" n="1368" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/3–3151: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chairman of the United
                        States Delegation to the Special Session of the Contracting Parties to GATT
                    </hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corse</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps"> niact </hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-03-31T17:00:00-05:00">March 31, 1951—5
                            p. m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>527. Re urtel 627 March 31.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d554-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>1. Agree line ur para III.</p>
                <pb facs="1385" n="1369" xml:id="pg1369"/>
                <p>2. Object to Melander proposal para I<hi rendition="#italic">d</hi> as worst of
                    various alternatives. Idea having two groups, one Paris and other Geneva,
                    working on same basic issue, not calculated produce results.</p>
                <p>3. Re ur para V. Prefer Brit proposal to no working party at all. Suggest you
                    concentrate amendment efforts on objective having WP in Paris.</p>
                <p>4. Above ITP views only.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d554-f2"/> Impossible obtain
                    interagency views in time for useful comments.</p>
                <p>Sent to USDel, Torquay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Achesok</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d554-f1" n="1" xml:id="d554-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d554-f2" n="2" xml:id="d554-f2-content">
                <p>That is, the views of the Office of International Trade Policy, Department of
                    State, rather than the collective opinion of the several interested agencies of
                    the government.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
